    "tiersNote": "G4 rival tiers. The block above IS the `works` tier - it is not copied here, so the calibrated G1 pace and the tier the game loads for `works` cannot drift apart. `rookie` and `feral` author only what they change: a cruise speed and the boost windows, per profile. Everything else (cornerSpeedGain, cornerSpeedFloor, noBlockSide, driftCurvature, straightCurvature) is inherited, so a later pass at the shared model moves all three tiers together. There is no runtime multiplier on speed anywhere - `applyPaceTier` in src/game/race-modes-rules.js merges these fields and nothing else. WINDOWS FIRST, CRUISE SECOND, and in that order for a reason: the windows are the authored driving character (rookie commits to a boost 30 m later off a corner and lets the launch boost go at 80% length; feral opens 30 m earlier and holds it 15 m longer), and the cruise is then SOLVED against those windows by `node scripts/rival-pace-calibration.mjs --tier=<tier> --solve` until the best rival lands in the phase's window. Solving cruise against a different set of windows than the race loads is how a calibrated number stops meaning anything. Measured on this tree, PRIVATEER 13 versus the demo player over five laps: rookie +3.24 s (greenwater) / +3.25 s (bitterpan), works -0.39 / -0.41, feral -3.24 / -3.26. scripts/validate-rivals.mjs pins all three.",
